{"id":3898,"date":"2021-10-25T13:54:10","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:54:10","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3898"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:30:58","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:30:58","slug":"2-5-loops-senior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-5-loops-senior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"2.5: Loops"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361eb92e\" name=\"6a221361eb92e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251447401{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361eba7e\" name=\"6a221361eba7e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are Loops?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_single_image image=&#8221;6353&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Loops<\/strong> let you repeat sections of your code. They\u2019re a great shortcut &#8212; without them, you might have to connect the same blocks over and over again! Blockly has three different types of loops:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>For loops<\/strong> will repeat the code inside them for the number of times you choose. There are two blocks that do this!\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>While loops<\/strong> will repeat the code inside them while a certain condition that you set is true. <\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Until loops<\/strong> will repeat the code inside them until a certain condition that you set is true.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12627&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebae6\" name=\"6a221361ebae6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>For Loops<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For loops repeat the code that\u2019s inside them for the number of times that you choose. Once that code has been repeated for that amount of time, your program will exit out of the loop and move on to the next block.<\/p>\n<p>Like we said in the first step, there are two for loop blocks in Blockly! One is the\u00a0<strong>repeat<\/strong>\u00a0block. To change the number in that block, you can just type in a new value. If you want to use a mathematical operation, equation, or variable, you can drag blocks from the math, logic, or variables menus to that gray area within the loop block.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12616&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]The other <strong>for loop<\/strong> block is a little more complicated and looks more like what you would see in text-based coding. With the\u00a0<strong>count<\/strong>\u00a0block, you would name a variable, and then you would set it to start at one number and go up to another. You can also set how much you want the value to increase by.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12609&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebb3e\" name=\"6a221361ebb3e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a For Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>Ready to try for loops out?<\/em> Program your CoDrone EDU to look like it\u2019s flying up a flight of stairs! The catch: since<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">there are two different for loop blocks, you will need to write two different programs to try them out. Your<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone EDU should keep moving forward and up. <em>The programs might look different to you, but what happens<\/em><\/span><em> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">when you run them?<\/span><\/em>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12630&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12631&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebbca\" name=\"6a221361ebbca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>While Loops<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]While loops repeat the code that\u2019s inside them while the condition that you set is true. Each time the program runs through the while loop, it checks to see if the condition is true. If it is not, your program will exit the loop.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10275&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebc4a\" name=\"6a221361ebc4a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a While Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You had your drone fly in a shape in the variables lesson, but now you can try it with a loop! Set your variable<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to 0, and then have it increase by 1 every time in the while loop. While your variable is less than 4, program<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">your CoDrone EDU to fly forward and then turn 90 degrees (or vice versa).<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>Wondering why you\u2019re starting at 0?<\/em> Humans begin counting at 1, but computers begin counting at 0!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7525&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebc97\" name=\"6a221361ebc97\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Until Loops<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Until loops are a lot like while loops, except they\u2019ll run the code inside the block until the condition is true. Each time the program runs through the while loop, it checks to see if the condition is true. If it is, the program will exit the loop, but after it finishes running that block of code one last time.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10277&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebcdb\" name=\"6a221361ebcdb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an Until Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Set your variable to 0, and then have it increase by 1 every time in the until loop. Program your drone so that until your variable gets to 3, it will yaw to the left for 1.5 seconds.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10278&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebd28\" name=\"6a221361ebd28\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenges<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Ride the Wave<\/b><\/p>\n<p>In this challenge, try programming your CoDrone EDU to fly in a wave shape. In other words, fly forward and repeat alternating the throttle to fly in a wave shape. Practice using loops with this challenge.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10279&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Challenge: Zigzag<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Use loops to program your CoDrone EDU to fly in a zigzag shape. Fly forward and alternative positive and negative roll. Don&#8217;t forget to use loops![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10280&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221361ebd6a\" name=\"6a221361ebd6a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this loops lesson, you learned how to utilize loops with various commands. Loops can also be placed inside other loops, creating &#8216;nested&#8217; loops that can repeat loops several times.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251447401{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-5-loops-senior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1817,1763,1777,1737,1815,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,4328,14401,2123,2118,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-3898","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-loops","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-intermediate","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3898","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":49,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3898\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[